Maybe--I think of the kind of Neo-Paganism I've seen in science fiction
fandom as the typical sort, and I count it as a non-religion religion
because of the emphasis on designing or choosing a lot of the religion
yourself.

At this point, I think of Gardnerian-style Paganism as Wicca and not
Neo-Pagan because the Gardnerians tend to be more hierarchical. Were 
they what you meant when you mentioned scripturally-based Neo-Pagans?

Just to get to something faintly more extropian-related, I've played
with the notion that the only religions which have a chance of being
trustworthy are those which have never been government religions....
it's a very short list--I think that all that's left at the moment
is Neo-Paganism and agnosticism. (Unitarianism was a state religion
in Transylvania and Buddhism was a state religion in some part of
India for a while. Actually, the Society of Friends (Quakers) might
count--I'm not sure what their relationship was to the government
of Pennsylvania.)

